MISSIONS

In September 2025, Conakry Terminal — a subsidiary of Africa Global Logistics — awarded two construction contracts for the extension of the Container Terminal of Conakry, including:
• the construction of a new 300 m long quay, founded at –14 m CD,
• the development of a 15 hectare reclaimed platform adjacent to the quay,
• and the extension of the port basin breakwater by 200 m.

The project scope is divided into a marine works package and a terrestrial works package, both supervised by a Project Management Consultant (PMC) responsible for:
• overall project consistency,
• compliance with the Employer’s Requirements,
• enforcement of HSSES rules across all stakeholders,
• and ensuring smooth and efficient project execution.

This project is of high strategic importance vis à vis public authorities; therefore, strict control of both schedule and budget is essential.

Reporting to the Project Director, you will be responsible for:
• Coordinating interactions between the Construction & Property Department at Head Office and the various project stakeholders;
• Monitoring the engineering firm in charge of project management services, as well as the contractors responsible for the works (quality control processes, deliverables, progress tracking, etc.);
• Providing support on ad hoc topics, including specific technical or coordination assignments as required.

PROFILE

- Graduate from an Engineering School, with a specialization in Civil Engineering; 
- Initial professional experience in industrial or civil works project management (internships and apprenticeships accepted); 
- Resilient in difficult environment 
- Curious, humble, resilient, adaptable and proactive, with a strong willingness to learn; 
- Comfortable working in an international and multicultural environment; 
- Fluent in English (B2–C1); Chinese is a plus; 
- A genuine interest in Africa is a strong asset.

